    {
      "id": "u05-1",
      "title": "The and a",
      "explanation": [
        "**die** = the. There's just one word for *the*, with no masculine or feminine.",
        "**'n** = a / an. It's always written with an apostrophe and said like a quick *uh*.",
        "At the start of a sentence, **'n** stays lower case and the next word gets the capital: **'n Man en 'n vrou.**"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Die hond is groot.",
          "en": "The dog is big."
        },
        {
          "af": "Die kat is klein.",
          "en": "The cat is small."
        },
        {
          "af": "'n Man en 'n vrou.",
          "en": "A man and a woman."
        },
        {
          "af": "Die kind is moeg.",
          "en": "The child is tired."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "die",
        "'n",
        "man",
        "vrou",
        "kind",
        "hond",
        "kat",
        "groot",
        "klein"
      ],
      "exercises": [
